{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Behold.</b> These shall come from afar, from the east:" "<b>[From the north].</b> This is Babylon:" "<b>And from the west.</b> Assyria, as it is written, \"and the king of Assyria turned their heart\" (Ezra 6:22):" "<b>From the land of Sinim.</b> From the direction of Egypt. Perhaps סינים (Sinim) is from this root [סנה]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {3 "The last clause reads הסנה מזאת הגזירה, which I render hyper-literally; the syntax and meaning of מזאת הגזירה are unclear — possibly 'from this root/derivation,' but the phrase is textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:45.316870427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}